<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Unilever cut at SBC Warburg.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Unilever cut at SBC Warburg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unilever Plc, the Anglo-Dutch foods and household products group, was cut to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot; at SBC Warburg, market sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The stock was down 10p at 13.82-1/2 stg by 1301 GMT, in moderate trading of 2.06 million shares. The stock reached a record 14.12 stg on September 17.</p>
<p>Sources said Warburg had downgraded its rating on Unilever in response to its sharp rise since the brokerage raised it to a &quot;buy&quot; in June, when they were trading around 12.20 stg.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
